    "narrative": "The spotlight today rests squarely on **Bryce Harper**, who secures our highest efficiency rating at 65.62. Facing Mahle, **Bryce Harper** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the three-hole and an advantageous matchup against a middle-of-the-road arm with a 4.01 xERA. While **Yainer Diaz** earns a functional start at 50.18, his output is tempered slightly by a neutral park factor and a mid-order slot against Burke. Meanwhile, **Justin Crawford** maintains his utility as a speed-based asset; despite hitting eighth, he earns a 54.93 score driven by a robust 7% platoon advantage, providing the necessary stolen base upside required to maintain our competitive edge in the standings.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's bench was excluding **Braden Montgomery**, whose score of 39.83 fell just short of our 40-point floor. While **Braden Montgomery**\u2019s switch-hitting versatility typically plays well, the negative park adjustments and a suboptimal eighth-place slot against Brown rendered him a risk to our efficiency targets. Elsewhere, the roster remains static with stalwarts like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Kyle Karros** either resting or ineligible for today\u2019s slate. Notably, **Cal Raleigh** and **Lawrence Butler** are unavailable due to team off-days, while **Tyler Freeman** remains in the minors, leaving our limited active group to carry the weight. Monitor the lineup environment closely, as any late defensive shifts could compress the values of our lower-order hitters like **Justin Crawford**.",
